          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.266,
            0.293,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.297,
            0.848,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Suppose you are using the number system that uses sticks to represent numbers, as in Method 1. Without using either the number names or the numerals of the Hindu number system, give a method for adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing two numbers or two collections of sticks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.397,
            0.579,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Suppose we have two groups of sticks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.417,
            0.579,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Count the sticks in each of the groups."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.437,
            0.738,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To add, put all sticks at one place and count altogether."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.457,
            0.845,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To subtract, take out sticks from the given collection of sticks and count the remaining sticks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.497,
            0.845,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To multiply two numbers, groups of equal numbers of sticks may be counted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.535,
            0.847,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For division, from the given number of sticks, the sticks in required number may be grouped. See the number of such groups formed and the number of ungrouped sticks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.606,
            0.847,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. One way of extending the number system in Method 2 is by using strings with more than one letter—for example, we could use ‘aa’ for 27. How can you extend this system to represent all the numbers? There are many ways of doing it!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.687,
            0.405,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Total alphabets = 26"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.708,
            0.403,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "One of the ways is –"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.727,
            0.721,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a, b, c, d, …, z and aa, bb, cc, …, zz and extend further."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.768,
            0.275,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": [
